# oracle: compute pace with bikflag 0 on a group (types 1 and 3 of the 161-atom H/N/O cell of PACKAGES/pace/compute) under pair_style pace with the same coupling_coefficients.yace: the summed descriptor row, the 3N gradient rows with the forces and the six virial rows with the pressure in the reference column, eight columns written by fix ave/time mode vector
# Native reference: LAMMPS b332f28 built with PKG_ML-PACE (the installed binary has no ML-PACE; see w257pace_recursive)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native: thermo 1.3e-14, written array file 2.2e-13.
# oracle-examples: PACKAGES/pace/compute/latte_cell_0.data PACKAGES/pace/compute/coupling_coefficients.yace
# oracle-files: w276cp_compute_pace_bik0.dat
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 filerel=1e-8
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     map hash
read_data       latte_cell_0.data
mass            1 1.00
mass            2 14.00
mass            3 15.999
pair_style      pace
pair_coeff      * * coupling_coefficients.yace H N O
group           HO type 1 3
compute         pace HO pace coupling_coefficients.yace 0 0
fix             cols all ave/time 1 1 1 c_pace[1] c_pace[17] c_pace[91] c_pace[92] c_pace[150] c_pace[183] c_pace[260] c_pace[274] mode vector file w276cp_compute_pace_bik0.dat format " %.15g"
thermo          1
thermo_style    custom step pe press c_pace[1][183] c_pace[1][274] c_pace[2][5] c_pace[485][274] c_pace[490][100]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
